{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
  "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Daniel R. Ortiz",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In asking this Court to cabin Connick v. Myers' public concern requirement, Respondent would constitutionalize, under the Petition Clause, large parts of the law of public employee discipline, and thereby grant to public employees a broad constitutional employment right that private employees do not enjoy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You agree that the Petition Clause is -- is different and does have a separate content?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Joseph R. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PALMORE: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Third Circuit rule here at issue is flawed for two fundamental reasons. First, contrary to this Court's admonitions, it quite literally constitutionalizes the employee grievance process by supplanting carefully calibrated nonconstitutional safeguards and by providing a potential First Amendment claim in Federal court to any employee who has filed a grievance on a matter of only private interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How about if they don't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you still apply Connick, just as speech on matters of private concern is protected by the First Amendment, yet under Connick, an employee who engages in speech on a matter of private concern is not going to be protected in the employment context in all respects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Suppose a State legislature passes a law depriving all State employees of collective bargaining rights, and a State employee files a lawsuit saying that this law violates the State constitution, and the State employee is thereupon fired. Is that a matter of public concern or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Neither the text, history, or purpose of the Petition Clause nor the interest of a government employer in an efficient workplace provide a basis for distinguishing and giving less protection to a petition because it didn't involve a matter of public concern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no further questions, we ask the judgment be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Then you have to offer a test and you don't want the public concern test, so what's your test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just white out \"Speech Clause\" and put in \"Petition Clause\" and file the same opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Mr. Schnapper, can I ask Justice Kennedy's question in maybe a little bit of a different way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if a number of municipal employees prepare a formal document called \"Petition,\" and they say: We have a grievance, and our grievance is that the quality of the food in the cafeteria is poor? Now, is that protected by the Petition Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You do, I think, recognize that it would be possible then to circumvent Connick if you could turn around and file a pleading and say: Now I have a petition, not just a grievance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schnapper",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0008",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, the Petitioners have in -- in highly expressive language described the decision in Filippo as one which would lead to an avalanche, tsunami, an overwhelming number of new lawsuits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1476",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "45502f0d3635047ff17c66edf4cf7e45ccf5f51aa301b77fa3246d0a93d6e311",
      "evidence_id": "ev-45502f0d3635-0002-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
